A||||2||Cliff D.||Sensor mods for racing, need ideas||||
Z||000000||Cliff D.||09-08-1999||09:45 AM||||I just aquired an '85 GT to build a race car out of. I will be running in scca's "improved touring" class. I am reading the rules here and this one has me baffled.<BR> "Fuel-injected cars may alter fuel mixture through the modification of the resistance values of the sensors which feed the computer. The computer shall remain unaltered."<BR> I can pretty much eliminate anything that has to do with emissions control and I can do some cool things (pun inteded) to the water management. God knows what the computer will think of that, but does anyone have a clue how to make my car faster by altering the values of the other sensors.||||reg||
Z||000001||lowCG||09-08-1999||01:56 PM||||You can alter what the computer percieves as an input by adding an adjustable(pot)of say,1.5K in series with the temp sensor.<BR>This will change the fuel pressure,spray pattern of the fuel injector(s).This is a very limited form of adjustment,and usually is most effective on a stock,or close to stock motor with exhaust changes only.<BR>I've tried this with the 4cyl.cars with success,however,haven't done anything to my 6cyl.<BR>A professional balance job,and match porting will help also.||||reg||
Z||000002||mwbackus||09-09-1999||03:54 PM||||If you are really serious about this, then you may as well do it the right way.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.venom-performance.com/v400.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.venom-performance.com/v400.htm</A> <P><BR>Mike<BR>Red 88 Formula||||reg||
